{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c423","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07721-ca06-7081-babf-b563190d8d78"},"sequence":108,"recorded_at":1780531400000211,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"98814c42-6a9f-4d46-909d-69c23fc4a002"},"task_id":"98814c42-6a9f-4d46-909d-69c23fc4a002","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"98814c42-6a9f-4d46-909d-69c23fc4a002","chunk":"Read text file `internal/secprim/env.go`.\n1|package secprim\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"sort\"\n5|\t\"strings\"\n6|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n7|)\n8|\n9|// IsEnvName reports whether name satisfies the environment-name grammar\n10|// shared by launch allowlists and SpawnPlan admission:\n11|// [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}. internal/provhost delegates its wire-plan\n12|// name check to this function, so the two packages cannot drift on what a\n13|// name is; the byte-counted plan bounds around it stay in provhost.\n14|func IsEnvName(name string) bool {\n15|\tif len(name) < 1 || len(name) > 128 {\n16|\t\treturn false\n17|\t}\n18|\tfor index := 0; index < len(name); index++ {\n19|\t\tchar := name[index]\n20|\t\tvalid := char == '_' ||\n21|\t\t\tchar >= 'A' && char <= 'Z' ||\n22|\t\t\tchar >= 'a' && char <= 'z' ||\n23|\t\t\tindex > 0 && char >= '0' && char <= '9'\n24|\t\tif !valid {\n25|\t\t\treturn false\n26|\t\t}\n27|\t}\n28|\treturn true\n29|}\n30|\n31|// BuildEnv builds the exact environment of a child process from a minimal\n32|// allowlist plus operator literals (Section 16.7 \"minimal environment\n33|// allowlists\"):\n34|//\n35|//   - allowed names the inherited variables the child may see. Each must\n36|//     satisfy IsEnvName; duplicates are refused rather than silently\n37|//     collapsed, because a duplicated allowlist entry is a configuration\n38|//     error. A name absent from lookup is skipped, not failed: an unset\n39|//     variable is a legitimate absence, while a failed read must never\n40|//     masquerade as one, so lookup reports only what it read.\n41|//   - literals carries explicit key=value pairs (workspace-derived values,\n42|//     SpawnPlan literals). Keys must satisfy IsEnvName and must be disjoint\n43|//     from allowed: a literal that shadows an inherited name would make the\n44|//     child's environment depend on map order rather than on policy.\n45|//   - values must be NUL-free valid UTF-8. Empty values are admitted:\n46|//     FOO= is a meaningful empty assignment, not a missing one.\n47|//\n48|// The result is sorted by name and rendered k=v, so identical inputs build\n49|// byte-identical environments. lookup abstracts the parent environment for\n50|// tests; production passes os.LookupEnv.\n51|//\n52|// No length bound is enforced here: the Section 5.1 literal bounds apply\n53|// to the SpawnPlan wire object in internal/provhost. No default allowlist\n54|// is declared here either: with no provider implementation in this\n55|// repository to derive runtime needs from, a baked-in list would be an\n56|// invented product policy, so the operator supplies the list explicitly\n57|// and ExecRunner inherits the parent environment until one is supplied.\n58|func BuildEnv(allowed []string, literals map[string]string, lookup func(string) (string, bool)) ([]string, error) {\n59|\tif lookup == nil {\n60|\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env lookup missing\", \"no parent environment reader\")\n61|\t}\n62|\tseen := make(map[string]bool, len(allowed))\n63|\tfor _, name := range allowed {\n64|\t\tif !IsEnvName(name) {\n65|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env name\", name)\n66|\t\t}\n67|\t\tif seen[name] {\n68|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env allowlist duplicate\", name)\n69|\t\t}\n70|\t\tseen[name] = true\n71|\t}\n72|\tfor key := range literals {\n73|\t\tif !IsEnvName(key) {\n74|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env name\", key)\n75|\t\t}\n76|\t\tif seen[key] {\n77|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env literal collision\", key)\n78|\t\t}\n79|\t}\n80|\tvalues := make(map[string]string, len(allowed)+len(literals))\n81|\tfor _, name := range allowed {\n82|\t\tvalue, present := lookup(name)\n83|\t\tif !present {\n84|\t\t\tcontinue\n85|\t\t}\n86|\t\tif strings.ContainsRune(value, 0) {\n87|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env value NUL\", name)\n88|\t\t}\n89|\t\tif !utf8.ValidString(value) {\n90|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env value encoding\", name)\n91|\t\t}\n92|\t\tvalues[name] = value\n93|\t}\n94|\tfor key, value := range literals {\n95|\t\tif strings.ContainsRune(value, 0) {\n96|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env value NUL\", key)\n97|\t\t}\n98|\t\tif !utf8.ValidString(value) {\n99|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env value encoding\", key)\n100|\t\t}\n101|\t\tvalues[key] = value\n102|\t}\n103|\tnames := make([]string, 0, len(values))\n104|\tfor name := range values {\n105|\t\tnames = append(names, name)\n106|\t}\n107|\tsort.Strings(names)\n108|\tenvironment := make([]string, 0, len(names))\n109|\tfor _, name := range names {\n110|\t\tenvironment = append(environment, name+\"=\"+values[name])\n111|\t}\n112|\treturn environment, nil\n113|}"}}}
