{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c56d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07721-ca06-7081-babf-b563190d8d78"},"sequence":273,"recorded_at":1780531400000541,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"dc4be433-17be-489a-a631-4fe35a3f4f10"},"task_id":"dc4be433-17be-489a-a631-4fe35a3f4f10","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"dc4be433-17be-489a-a631-4fe35a3f4f10","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-4-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls internal/secprim/*.go | head -n 30; echo \\\"===\\\"; cat internal/secprim/doc.go; echo \\\"===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"Emit\\\\|Progress\\\\|Prompt\\\" internal/cliresult/*.go | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect cliresult wiring and doc\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"internal/secprim/argv_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/argv.go\\ninternal/secprim/census_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/classes_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/doc.go\\ninternal/secprim/env_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/env.go\\ninternal/secprim/errors.go\\ninternal/secprim/fifo_unix_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/inventory_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/nofollow.go\\ninternal/secprim/open_nofollow_unix.go\\ninternal/secprim/open_nofollow_windows.go\\ninternal/secprim/path_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/path.go\\ninternal/secprim/priv_windows_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/redact_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/redact.go\\ninternal/secprim/render_test.go\\ninternal/secprim/render.go\\n===\\n// Package secprim implements the AX shared safe process and filesystem\\n// primitives of pinned specification Sections 16.3, 16.4, and 16.7: no-follow\\n// path handling, staging containment, structured argv, environment\\n// allowlists, terminal control-string escaping, and secret redaction for\\n// free-text streams.\\n//\\n// The package is a library behind production launch and rendering paths,\\n// not a second authority beside them:\\n//\\n//   - path grammars stay in internal/scalar: CheckMemberPath admits exactly\\n//     the scalar relative-path grammar plus the Windows alternate-stream,\\n//     trailing-dot/space, and reserved-device rules Section 16.3 names, and\\n//     delegates every shared rule to scalar rather than retyping it;\\n//   - byte-counted exec rules (Provider SpawnPlan argv and env literals,\\n//     Section 5.1) stay in internal/provhost: that package validates the\\n//     wire plan, while this package builds the launch environment and\\n//     validates the argv vector at process start;\\n//   - environment-name grammar is owned here and internal/provhost delegates\\n//     to it, so the two packages cannot drift on what a name is;\\n//   - Structured Error detail redaction stays in internal/axerror: that\\n//     package refuses exact credential keys and causal leaks on the error\\n//     wire, while this package scrubs free-text streams (stderr, logs,\\n//     terminal rendering) where no key gate can see;\\n//   - SSH argv admission stays in internal/config and the provider entry\\n//     point rule (`ax pane SESSION_ID`) stays in internal/terminalbackend:\\n//     both are closed vocabularies over their own domain, not instances of\\n//     the generic argv rule here;\\n//   - the five-variable AX_* path registry stays in internal/config and\\n//     internal/localstore, which already implement AC-PATH-001.\\n//\\n// Trust for external executables is deliberately not implemented here.\\n// internal/provider.trustCandidate and internal/terminalbackend.DigestFile\\n// already establish trust with different fact sets because their\\n// specifications differ: Section 7.1 requires the approving owner identity\\n// beside the canonical path and digest for provider plugins, while the\\n// Section 4.B trust tuple carries platform, adapter identity, manifest and\\n// probe digests with no owner fact. A third path here would be another\\n// copy, not convergence; the difference is contractual, not accidental.\\n//\\n// Every refusal is a plain *Error naming the kind, rule, and member:\\n// facades keep their own refusal dialects, so this package names rules\\n// instead of minting codes, following internal/environ.\\n//\\n// Stated bounds. This package mutates no durable state and keeps no cache:\\n// Guard resolution is lexical, OpenNoFollowFile opens read-only, and every\\n// other entry point is a pure function of its input. Crash and idempotency\\n// handling therefore have no surface here: there is no journal to recover\\n// and no second actor to collide with. Tombstone deletion scope (Section\\n// 16.3 \\\"broad deletion from tombstones\\\") has no implementation in this\\n// repository yet and is not modeled. The operator default for which\\n// environment names a provider plugin inherits is product policy with no\\n// in-repo provider implementation to derive needs from, so BuildEnv takes\\n// the allowlist explicitly and ExecRunner inherits the parent environment\\n// until the operator supplies one. Grapheme-width policing stops at the\\n// enumerated invisible controls: full East-Asian/emoji width measurement\\n// needs terminal width tables this package does not carry. Content-level\\n// secret scrubbing is best-effort by specification (Section 16.2 claims no\\n// reliable scrubbing), and Redact states exactly the three shapes it\\n// decides.\\npackage secprim\\n===\\ninternal/cliresult/bodies_test.go:512:// TestLogsBodyBindsEveryEventToItsEmitter narrows the Section 14.1 sentence\\ninternal/cliresult/bodies_test.go:515:func TestLogsBodyBindsEveryEventToItsEmitter(t *testing.T) {\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:15:// mustEmittedFailure renders one failure through the production emitter in JSON\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:18:// test are the bytes Emit wrote, not a literal a test composed.\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:19:func mustEmittedFailure(t *testing.T, code axerror.Code) (InvocationOutput, string) {\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:22:\\temitter := mustEmitter(t, ModeJSON, true, streams.streams(true))\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:26:\\tif _, err := emitter.Progress(\\\"transferring 3 of 9\\\"); err != nil {\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:27:\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"Progress: %v\\\", err)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:29:\\tstatus, err := emitter.Emit(Outcome{Failure: mustFailure(t, code)})\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:31:\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"Emit: %v\\\", err)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:36:func mustEmittedSuccess(t *testing.T, command Command) InvocationOutput {\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:39:\\temitter := mustEmitter(t, ModeJSON, true, streams.streams(false))\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:40:\\tstatus, err := emitter.Emit(Outcome{Result: mustResult(t, validSpec(t, command))})\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:42:\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"Emit: %v\\\", err)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:61:\\t\\tdocuments[command] = mustEmittedSuccess(t, command)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:104:\\toutput, stderr := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"workspace_conflict\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:140:\\t// The mutant: stdout and stderr are swapped, so Emit's one JSON document\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:143:\\temitter := mustEmitter(t, ModeJSON, true, misrouted)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:144:\\tstatus, err := emitter.Emit(Outcome{Failure: mustFailure(t, \\\"workspace_conflict\\\")})\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:146:\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"Emit: %v\\\", err)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:167:\\tvalid, _ := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"workspace_conflict\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:378:\\tfailure, _ := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"workspace_conflict\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:379:\\tsuccess := mustEmittedSuccess(t, CommandList)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:560:\\tconforming := mustEmittedSuccess(t, CommandList)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:652:\\tlegacy, _ := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"not_found\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:675:\\tlegacy, _ := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"not_found\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:686:\\tsuccess := mustEmittedSuccess(t, CommandList)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:789:\\tlegacy, _ := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"not_found\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:830:\\toriginal, _ := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"workspace_conflict\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:900:\\tfailure, _ := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"not_found\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:964:\\treading, err := Read(CommandList, mustEmittedSuccess(t, CommandList))\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:1035:\\tsuccess := mustEmittedSuccess(t, CommandList)\\ninternal/cliresult/client_test.go:1223:\\tlegacy, _ := mustEmittedFailure(t, \\\"not_found\\\")\\ninternal/cliresult/cliresult_test.go:174:// TestUnimplementedSurfacesAreRefusedRatherThanEmitted proves that a registered\\ninternal/cliresult/cliresult_test.go:178:func TestUnimplementedSurfacesAreRefusedRatherThanEmitted(t *testing.T) {\\ninternal/cliresult/confirmation_test.go:33:// TestInteractiveDestructiveOperationMustPrompt narrows the Section 14.2\\ninternal/cliresult/confirmation_test.go:36:func TestInteractiveDestructiveOperationMustPrompt(t *testing.T) {\\ninternal/cliresult/confirmation_test.go:48:\\tif !confirmation.PromptRequired {\\ninternal/cliresult/confirmation_test.go:60:\\tif refusal != nil || !confirmation.PromptRequired {\\ninternal/cliresult/confirmation_test.go:90:\\tif confirmation.PromptRequired {\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8258,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2065,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
