{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07721-ca06-7081-babf-b563190d8d78"},"sequence":571,"recorded_at":1780531400001137,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"412a806a-b867-4f69-b2fd-a36074d7dc66"},"task_id":"412a806a-b867-4f69-b2fd-a36074d7dc66","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"412a806a-b867-4f69-b2fd-a36074d7dc66","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2ciy0s/TASK-260830-2ciy0s_secprim.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2ciy0s — safe path/argv/environment primitives (outcome)\n2|\n3|Leaf 1 of STORY-260830-1i3qu7. New shared library `internal/secprim`\n4|(Sections 16.3, 16.4, 16.7) plus production wiring into the provider\n5|launch path and the CLI render path. Work left UNCOMMITTED in the story\n6|worktree on top of trunk `157a54c`; no commits made by this leaf.\n7|\n8|## Production entry points (call sites)\n9|\n10|- `internal/secprim/doc.go` — scope, reuse map, trust-path\n11|  non-duplication rationale, stated bounds.\n12|- `internal/secprim/path.go` — `CheckMemberPath`, `Guard.NewGuard` /\n13|  `Resolve`, `DetectCaseCollision`, `CheckRegularTarget`.\n14|- `internal/secprim/nofollow.go` (+ `open_nofollow_unix.go`) —\n15|  `OpenNoFollowFile`, `OpenNoFollowDir` (Windows file:\n16|  `open_nofollow_windows.go`, Lstat gate with stated TOCTOU bound).\n17|- `internal/secprim/argv.go` — `CheckArgv`, `Command.NewCommand`.\n18|- `internal/secprim/env.go` — `IsEnvName`, `BuildEnv`.\n19|- `internal/secprim/render.go` — `EscapeForTerminal`,\n20|  `RenderForTerminal`.\n21|- `internal/secprim/redact.go` — `Redact` (corpus, PEM, key=value,\n22|  URL userinfo).\n23|- Wiring 1: `internal/provhost/runner.go` — `ExecRunner.Env`\n24|  (nil inherits; non-nil replaces wholesale, built by `BuildEnv`) and\n25|  `CheckArgv` validation of the executable at start.\n26|- Wiring 2: `internal/provhost/spawn.go` — `validEnvName` now delegates\n27|  to `secprim.IsEnvName` (one grammar, two call sites).\n28|- Wiring 3: `internal/cliresult/output.go` — `Log`, `Progress`,\n29|  `Prompt`, and text-mode `Emit` cross `terminalLine`\n30|  (`RenderForTerminal`); JSON mode stays byte-exact.\n31|- Extension: `internal/scalar/path.go` — exported\n32|  `IsReservedWindowsDeviceName` for the member gate (same table the\n33|  absolute-path gate uses).\n34|\n35|## Reuse / non-duplication record\n36|\n37|- Scalar relative/absolute grammars (incl. recursive encoded\n38|  separators), environ (frames/identity/tuples), axerror detail +\n39|  causal-leak gates, config SSH admission, terminalbackend\n40|  `CheckEntrypoint`, localstore/config AX_* registry: all cited as\n41|  owners in `doc.go`; none re-implemented.\n42|- Trust: NO third path. `provider.trustCandidate` carries canonical\n43|  path + digest + approving owner identity per Section 7.1;\n44|  `terminalbackend.DigestFile` + trust tuple carry platform/adapter/\n45|  manifest/probe digests with no owner fact per Section 4.B. The\n46|  difference is contractual (spec clauses differ), not accidental.\n47|- `IsEnvName` is the one deliberate convergence: provhost delegated to\n48|  the new owner rather than keeping a second copy.\n49|\n50|## Coverage — Section 16 MUST rows: 16 of 25 driven, 9 bounds/pre-existing\n51|\n52|Fully driven through production entries (13): untrusted-member\n53|grammar, traversal, absolute, drive/UNC, alternate streams,\n54|encoded separators (+encoded-dot/overlong extension),\n55|symlink/reparse escape at validation and commit, case-fold\n56|collisions, unmanaged replacement, device/FIFO/socket refusal,\n57|argv-array/no-shell, terminal render escaping, TOCTOU dir-handle\n58|primitives (unix).\n59|Partially driven — gate wired, consumer or policy bound (3):\n60|stderr/log redaction (key/PEM arms wired into the emitter; corpus arm\n61|tested, no in-repo secret corpus yet), launch environment\n62|(allowlist builder + runner field wired; default policy unset —\n63|inherits until supplied), structured launch (argv+env new; fixed\n64|`ax pane` entry and cwd launcher pre-existing/absent).\n65|Pre-existing owners, cited not re-driven (3): SSH fixed entry +\n66|encoding (config), plugin trust (provider/terminalbackend), plugin\n67|stdout validation (provhost).\n68|Declared bounds, no in-repo path at M0 (6): tombstone deletion\n69|scope, archive staging root + re-validation after extraction,\n70|clone-bundle exclusions, metric labels, audit retention, cwd policy.\n71|\n72|Section 19.4 security ACs: AC-SEC-003 and AC-DIR-TERM-001 driven at\n73|gate level (member/symlink/case/special-file/command-injection\n74|refusals; hostile-render inertness; argv/env admission); AC-SEC-001,\n75|AC-DIR-SEC-001, AC-OBS-001, AC-V043-SEC-001 are bounds (no\n76|transfer/record/metric/log implementations to exclude from);\n77|AC-SEC-002, AC-PATH-001, AC-PATH-002 are pre-existing owners\n78|(config, localstore).\n79|\n80|Crash/idempotency: no surface. The package is pure functions plus\n81|read-only opens plus terminal writes; it mutates no durable state,\n82|keeps no cache, owns no journal.\n83|\n84|## Mutant battery: applied 15, killed 15, NOT_APPLIED 0, COMPILE_FAIL 1*\n85|\n86|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to | Named failing test |\n87||---|---|---|\n88|| M1 drop encoded-dot arm | admits exactly `%2e` members | TestCheckMemberPathRefuses/encoded_dot* (4 subtests) |\n89|| M2 drop ADS arm | admits exactly `ab:c` on Windows | …/windows_ads, …/windows_ads_nested |\n90|| M3 drop device-name arm | admits exactly CON/LPT… | …/windows_con* (5 subtests) |\n91|| M4 drop argv NUL arm | admits exactly NUL argv | …/nul_executable, …/nul_argument |\n92|| M5 drop literal-collision arm | admits exactly shadowing literals | TestBuildEnvRefuses/literal_collides |\n93|| M6 drop DEL arm | admits exactly DEL | …/del + OutputBytes sweep |\n94|| M7 drop bidi arm | admits exactly U+202A–U+202E | …/bidi_override + OutputBytes sweep |\n95|| M8 drop `password` scrub key | admits exactly that key | TestSensitiveKeyListIsReviewed + …/equals, json_pair, case_folded, json_spaced |\n96|| M9 redact every BEGIN block (widening) | certificates redacted | TestRedactPrivateKeyBlocks |\n97|| M10 drop managed-set arm | admits unmanaged replacement | TestGuardManagedSet (audit stays green — derivation follows source; recorded split) |\n98|| M11 token-preserving shell (`\"s\"+\"h\"` + os/exec, no literal) | static scan passes | TestPackageLaunchesNoProcess (behavioral half kills it) |\n99|| M12 drop `secret` census token | secret-named sites underived | TestSecretSiteRosterIsComplete (orphans) |\n100|| M13a drop all terminalLine uses | — | COMPILE_FAIL (unused import; re-done as M13b) |\n101|| M13b drop Log-only wiring | raw Log output | TestTextEmissionNeutralizesHostileContent |\n102|| M14 ignore runner.Env | silent inheritance | TestExecRunnerDeliversExactlyTheBuiltEnv |\n103|| M15 rename class row | orphaned row | TestExclusionClassRosterIsComplete |\n104|\n105|\\* M13a is the single COMPILE_FAIL entry: removing every use broke the\n106|import. It was re-applied narrowly (M13b) and killed. No survivors:\n107|every surviving-mutant question is answered by a named failing test.\n108|\n109|## Gates (real exit codes, standalone processes)\n110|\n111|- `go test ./... -count=1` → exit 0 (20 packages ok; log attached).\n112|- `go test secprim+provhost+cliresult+scalar -race -count=1` → exit 0.\n113|- `go test ./... -cover` → exit 0 (secprim 94.5%, provhost 85.8%,\n114|  cliresult 95.5%, scalar 90.1%).\n115|- `go vet ./...` → exit 0. `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` → exit 0\n116|  (after adding the Windows fifo stub; unix-only failure was\n117|  `makeFifo` undefined — fixed, re-verified).\n118|- `gofmt -l internal/` → clean. `tracecheck` → exit 0, figures\n119|  unchanged (94 acceptance cases; none added to the registry by this\n120|  leaf — the conformance-CI leaf owns the gate).\n121|\n122|## Residue (explicit bounds, not hidden)\n123|\n124|1. Windows no-follow is check-then-open (no O_NOFOLLOW in Go);\n125|   owner-only staging roots narrow the race; stated in code.\n126|2. Corpus redaction needs a caller-known secret list; no in-repo\n127|   caller holds credentials yet (no config credential fields, no\n128|   logger/doctor). `RenderForTerminal(line, nil)` still applies\n129|   key/PEM arms everywhere wired.\n130|3. Compound keys outside the 27 (`db_password`), bare `key`/`auth`/\n131|   `pwd`, non-PEM key material, combining-mark floods, emoji width:\n132|   explicitly out of the scrubber/escaper; corpus arm is the fallback.\n133|4. `auth`-substring declarations are outside the census instrument\n134|   (Authority blind spot, pinned by TestSecretScanBlindSpot);\n135|   `auth_json`/non-derived table keys are covered behaviorally by\n136|   TestSecretAxerrorTableRefused instead.\n137|5. Operator default allowlist policy is unset (inherit until\n138|   supplied); provider needs cannot be derived with no provider\n139|   implementation in-repo.\n140|6. Guard/OpenNoFollow have no in-repo staging/extraction consumer yet\n141|   (no archive code at M0); the storage-boundary leaf\n142|   (TASK-260830-3qrfjp) is the designated first consumer.\n143|\n144|## Follow-ups for the orchestrator (no board elements created)\n145|\n146|- F1: storage-boundary leaf should consume Guard/OpenNoFollowFile\n147|  for staging/extraction when archive code lands.\n148|- F2: provider-conformance leaf should set the ExecRunner allowlist\n149|  policy (which names) once provider runtime needs are known.\n150|- F3: doctor/logging work should supply secret corpora to\n151|  RenderForTerminal/Redact at persistence points.\n152|- F4: conformance-CI leaf owns traceability-registry additions for\n153|  the new AC-level gates (this leaf added none).\n154|\n155|## Tree state\n156|\n157|HEAD `157a54c` unchanged (no commits). Modified: README.md,\n158|internal/cliresult/output.go, internal/provhost/{inventory_test,\n159|runner, spawn}.go, internal/scalar/{path,scalar_test}.go. Added: internal/secprim/ (10 prod + 10 test files; 42 tests + 84 subtests green),\n160|internal/cliresult/render_wiring_test.go,\n161|internal/provhost/{env_agreement,runner_env}_test.go."}}}
