{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d40b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07721-ca06-7081-babf-b563190d8d78"},"sequence":2144,"recorded_at":1780531400004283,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"50f170fc-f3d7-4451-a144-0437055d4e1b"},"task_id":"50f170fc-f3d7-4451-a144-0437055d4e1b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"50f170fc-f3d7-4451-a144-0437055d4e1b","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 535-562\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-`Guard.Resolve` maps one staging member to its commit path under the\n-lexical member grammar plus an independent joined-prefix check (the\n-prefix conjunct is unreachable through the entry and stays as defense\n-in depth, pinned by a generated-corpus tripwire), an optional managed\n-set, and Unicode case-fold collision detection;\n-`OpenNoFollowFile`/`OpenNoFollowDir` open without following a trailing\n-symlink (`O_NOFOLLOW` on unix; an owner-only Lstat gate with a stated\n-TOCTOU bound on Windows) and re-verify shape on the descriptor.\n-`Command` builds only from argv arrays — the package has no shell\n-constructor, proven by a token scan plus a behavioral no-`os/exec`\n-import gate that catches the token-preserving mutant.\n-`BuildEnv` builds the exact child environment from an allowlist plus\n-disjoint literals (absent names skipped, never defaulted), wired into\n-`provhost.ExecRunner.Env`, which inherits until the operator supplies a\n-list. `EscapeForTerminal` neutralizes ANSI/OSC, C0/C1 controls, DEL,\n-bidi overrides, zero-width characters, and invalid UTF-8 while keeping\n-newline, tab, and legitimate text (idempotent, so double-wiring is\n-safe), wired into every `cliresult` text path with JSON mode left\n-byte-exact. `Redact` scrubs caller-known secrets, private-key blocks,\n-sensitive `key=value` pairs, and URL userinfo; Section 16.2 claims no\n-reliable content-level scrubbing and neither does this package — the\n-bound is stated on the function. The secret-site census derives every\n-secret-named declaration, parameter, tag, and literal across the\n-secret-handling packages from syntax and requires a disposition row\n-with a verified witness for each, and the Section 16.2 class roster\n-derives all nine exclusion classes from the pinned document the same\n-way. The package mutates no durable state and keeps no cache, so it\n-has no crash or idempotency surface.\n+`Guard.Resolve` maps one staging member to its lexical commit path under\n+the member grammar plus an independent joined-prefix check (the prefix\n+conjunct is unreachable through the entry and stays as defense in\n+depth, pinned by a generated-corpus tripwire), an optional managed set,\n+and Unicode case-fold collision detection. Lexical resolution alone\n+does not contain: a symlinked intermediate directory redirects any\n+path-string open outside the root, because `O_NOFOLLOW` constrains only\n+the final component. The commit half is `Guard.Open`, which walks every\n+component relative to an `OpenNoFollowDir` root handle (`openat` with\n+`O_NOFOLLOW` per component on unix, never re-resolving a path string)\n+and refuses a symlinked parent at commit time as `member symlink\n+escape`. `OpenNoFollowFile`/`OpenNoFollowDir` open without following a\n+trailing symlink (`O_NOFOLLOW` on unix; an Lstat gate refusing symlinks\n+and irregular reparse points with a stated check-then-open TOCTOU bound\n+on Windows) and re-verify shape on the descriptor; the unix open sets\n+`O_NONBLOCK` so a FIFO refuses instead of stalling the opener.\n+`Command` builds only from argv arrays — the package has no shell\n+constructor, proven by a token scan plus a behavioral no-`os/exec`\n+import gate that catches the token-preserving mutant.\n+`BuildEnv` builds the exact child environment from an allowlist plus\n+disjoint literals (absent names skipped, never defaulted), wired into\n+`provhost.ExecRunner.Env`: nil inherits, an empty list denies all —\n+the two are tested as distinct obligations. `EscapeForTerminal`\n+neutralizes ANSI/OSC, C0/C1 controls, DEL, bidi overrides and isolates,\n+directional marks, zero-width characters, and invalid UTF-8 while\n+keeping newline, tab, and legitimate text (idempotent, so double-wiring\n+is safe), wired into all six `cliresult` text paths (`Log`, `Progress`,\n+interactive `Prompt`, the non-interactive refusal text, and both `Emit`\n+directions, each pinned by a hostile-content test) with JSON mode left\n+byte-exact. `Redact` scrubs caller-known secrets, private-key blocks,\n+sensitive `key=value` pairs, and URL userinfo; Section 16.2 claims no\n+reliable content-level scrubbing and neither does this package — the\n+bound is stated on the function. The secret-site census derives every\n+secret-named declaration, parameter, tag, and literal across the\n+secret-handling packages from syntax and requires a disposition row\n+with a verified witness for each (names outside the 13-token\n+vocabulary are outside the witness, stated as a bound), the Section\n+16.2 class roster derives all nine exclusion classes from the pinned\n+document the same way, and the five archive-`nopath` rows claim only\n+the bound the recursive import scan proves (no archive-writer import\n+anywhere under `internal/`, nested packages included — not the absence\n+of every non-archive emission shape). The refusal inventory derives all\n+41 constructor call sites and additionally fails on any refusal built\n+outside the constructors (aliases, literals, factories, value\n+escapes). Windows behavior is compile-and-vet only, never executed;\n+the Lstat reparse mapping is established from the Go runtime source\n+(`ModeSymlink` only for true symlinks, every other reparse point\n+surfacing as `ModeIrregular`, which the gate also refuses). The package\n+mutates no durable state and keeps no cache, so it has no crash or\n+idempotency surface.\n"}}}
