{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d667","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07721-ca06-7081-babf-b563190d8d78"},"sequence":2446,"recorded_at":1780531400004887,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38f2a4ef-6e71-4516-af44-8dd3ca8a69cd"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Round 2 is ready for review — handed off to review (`to-review`, checklist 18/18).\n\nAll eight findings closed:\n\n- **B1 (live escape):** new `Guard.Open` walks every component via `openat` with `O_NOFOLLOW` from the `OpenNoFollowDir` handle, never re-resolving a path string. The reviewer's fixture now refuses at commit as `member symlink escape` while lexical `Resolve` still admits — both halves pinned. Darwin's `ENOTDIR`-instead-of-`ELOOP` quirk is handled via descriptor-relative `fstatat`, fail-closed.\n- **B2 (FIFO hang):** `O_NONBLOCK` on the unix open; the opener is now driven through a FIFO with a hang-timeout test.\n- **B3:** success-`Emit`, `Progress`, and `Prompt`-refusal hostile-content tests added — all six text paths driven; README enumerates them.\n- **B4:** empty-`Env` deny-all proven through `/usr/bin/env` (byte-empty child env), distinct from nil-inherits.\n- **B5:** inventory derivation rewritten around alias fixpoint, literals, `new(Error)`, factories, and value escapes. Live plants A–D plus control all caught through the real audit; committed synthetic test covers eight shapes.\n- **B6:** corpus fed from the same 16-rune slice it asserts; per-rune rows added.\n- **B7:** recursive 110-file scan, fail-closed on parse errors; nested `archive/zip` plant caught; five `nopath` rows restated as archive-format bounds.\n- **B8:** 41 derived exits; narrowing battery 27/27 killed, deletions 15/15 killed (counted separately), survivors N7/R12 with stated bounds, N24 withdrawn as invalid, M13a kept separate. Tree verified byte-identical after the battery.\n\nGates, all run directly in this session: full suite exit 0 (20 packages), `go vet`/`GOOS=windows vet`/`GOOS=windows build` exit 0, `gofmt` clean, `-race` on touched packages green, secprim coverage 94.2%, tracecheck unchanged. AC corrected to 16 of 25 driven, 0 falsified. Outcome doc, rerunnable battery script, and full-test log attached as task-scoped resources. Work left uncommitted in the story worktree.","reason":null}}
